  "body": "Originally https://github.com/tmpvar/jsdom/issues/1566.\n\nIf I am reading [the steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#focus-update-steps) correctly, currently the blur event occurs in step 2, then changing of the focused area of the control group (and thus changing what activeElement returns) happens in step 4.2, and then firing focus events happens in step 4.5.\n\nHowever, @moll points out that in most browsers activeElement is updated during the blur event handlers: https://jsfiddle.net/dcuLhcd7/6/. Edge seems to follow the spec here (activeElement is the previously-focused element) while Chrome and Firefox do not (activeElement is always body in the blur handler).\n",
